<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97d595e88864fa0fe1e9b530996793423679d879bc4a76729e537d2382263330</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield after Leipzig attack: report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21b036ca2d3c780bd3e924f5e2ab67aa2dff44955325c5d8b91d3b5b7fed9016</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-after-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--16a7e978ba8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-after-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, Bild am Sonntag newspaper reported.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German company successfully launches rocket to space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:576212affbf541f2bf1105c23b4e3ed8716acd611be3ee463099f6f533e8c9e6</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717--59c961471bc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bavaria-based Isar Aerospace managed to launch its Spectrum rocket into orbit, 18 months after its first attempt. This is the first such launch from European soil.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd60035923213e097ad9864d8cda40e076a0038d18d5f2e2cdaf9e47ede9dcb9</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a14d4dca78bb2d6e23c224b32a44bea0e8ccfc7787b9af36c9b5f381bd37581</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, partners aim to finalize 'return hubs' by year end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba1b3cc0df021d005ca76c626d4ee556f91a851c4fa4510cb5cdf33ae72fcfed</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242--cc966167d922.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Dobrindt said "technical discussions" were underway with non-EU countries to establish controversial "return hubs." Rights organizations have questioned the legality and morality of the plans.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt's state election will have a nationwide impact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84807bef320bc5be5b0e6e7c4529a9cb4fa94b93a63a2955d5ad657805267e72</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T01:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569--8cf3f82cd3a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The parliamentary election in the small eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt could have dramatic consequences for Germany's federal government, further raising dissatisfaction with Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d722a670c3dfa99ddee3eb5f2a6289ca9a2ecdc7c7cc6913fde56cc644dcf224</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Germany heads into three elections in September, rumors are circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0384bc82c07c766722801ee7d0cf7b9f805a3e8e378ba8a51f01d0c6513c25f</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c201d81b3e0ecd076f22063da1e62cef3f25e16a37fff06f7ca7c6739eeec90b</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
